[center][size=6][b]TheExpanse[/b][/size]
[size=4]Room in the bay for oversized custom ships[/size]
[size=3]A mod for Hardspace: Shipbreaker · v0.4.0[/size][/center]

[line]

Some custom ships are too big for the work bay. To fit, they are posed to spawn above the bay's jacks, or at an angle. That works, but the ship hangs crooked or out of reach of the jacks.

This mod corrects it. Each custom ship is straightened, placed in the middle of the bay, and the jacks are moved out of its way. It also makes big rooms take longer to pressurize.

It was made for the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/hardspaceshipbreaker/mods/41]MCRN Corvette[/url] (the Tachi, the Rocinante and the Beratnas Gas Hauler), and works with any custom ship. The game's own ships are never touched, so the tutorial and story play as normal.


[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Straightens the ship.[/b] A ship posed at an angle is turned square to the bay. Nothing has to be set up: the mod reads the ship's own shape.
[*][b]Centres the ship.[/b] It is placed midway between the side walls, centred on the bay's height, with its rear end 10 metres in front of the back wall.
[*][b]Moves the jacks.[/b] The Master Jack is pushed along the bay until it is clear of the ship's far end. Its kiosk, its hab door and your start and respawn point go with it. The five light jacks are raised together until they clear the ship's top.
[*][b]Big rooms take longer to pressurize.[/b] The game fills and empties every room in about 5 seconds. With this mod, a room takes as long as the ship's author set it to.
[/list]

Everything is back in its normal place for the next ship.


[size=5][b]How straightening works[/b][/size]
There is no record of which way a ship should face, so its own shape is used:
[list]
[*]The tightest box that fits around the ship is found. Its long side is the ship's length, and the ship is turned so that this lies along the bay.
[*]If the ship's width and height are too alike to tell which way is up, its roll is taken from its mirror symmetry. The plane between its matching left and right halves is found and stood upright.
[/list]
The ship is always turned by the smallest amount that squares it up. A ship that is already square is not touched. A ship with no clear shape to go by (about as wide as it is long, and not symmetric) keeps the angle it is posed at.

This takes well under a second, once, while the ship loads.


[size=5][b]Saved ships[/b][/size]
A ship loaded from a save goes back where it was when you saved it. If you saved it straightened and centred, it loads that way. If you saved it before installing this mod, it loads where it was and is not moved.


[size=5][b]Room pressure times[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Only rooms set to longer than the game's own time are affected. Every other room, and every ship that leaves the times at their default, behaves as before.
[*]Rooms connected by open doors change pressure together and take the longest time among them.
[*]A hull breach still vents at the game's normal speed.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Hardspace: Shipbreaker
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases]BepInEx 5 (x64)[/url], not version 6 or above
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install BepInEx: extract it into the same folder as Shipbreaker.exe, run the game to the main menu, then quit.
[*]Download this mod and extract it into [b]BepInEx\plugins\[/b], so you end up with:
[code]Hardspace Shipbreaker\BepInEx\plugins\TheExpanse\me.kerballone.TheExpanse.dll[/code]
[/list]

To remove it, delete the [b]TheExpanse[/b] folder.


[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]
The settings file is created on first run:
[code]Hardspace Shipbreaker\BepInEx\config\me.kerballone.TheExpanse.cfg[/code]
It is read again each time a ship starts loading, so you can edit it while the game is running and the change applies to the next ship.
[list]
[*][b]Enabled[/b] (default true): turns the whole mod on or off.
[*][b]CenterShip[/b] (default true): place custom ships in the middle of the bay and move the jacks to suit.
[*][b]StraightenShip[/b] (default true): turn a custom ship square to the bay before centring it.
[*][b]StraightenRatio[/b] (default 1.5): how much longer one side of the ship has to be than the next before its direction is trusted.
[*][b]BackWallGapMeters[/b] (default 10): the gap between the back wall and the end of the ship nearest to it.
[*][b]AcrossOffsetMeters[/b] (default 0): how far to one side of the bay's middle ships are placed.
[*][b]BayCenterHeight[/b] (default 0): the height ships are centred on. Raise or lower it to sit ships higher or lower.
[*][b]ClearanceMeters[/b] (default 5): the gap kept between the ship and the jacks.
[*][b]MovePlayerSpawnWithMasterJack[/b] (default true): move your start and respawn point along with the Master Jack.
[*][b]UsePressureTimes[/b] (default true): make each room's own pressurization and decompression time count.
[/list]


[size=5][b]For ship authors[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]A ship too large for the bay can be posed above the jacks, or at an angle, so that it is playable without this mod. With the mod installed it is squared up and brought down into the bay. No special setup is needed.
[*]To make a room slow to pressurize or decompress, set [b]Pressurization Time[/b] and [b]Decompression Time[/b] on its room container, in seconds. Values of about 5 or less make no difference: the mod never makes a room faster than the game does.
[/list]


[size=5][b]Known limits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The ship's size is worked out before it spawns, so a centred ship can sit a little off. The BepInEx log reports how far after each load.
[*]For very long ships, roughly 180 metres and up, the Master Jack ends up beyond the edge of the playable area.
[*]This mod is at an early version and will gain more features.
[/list]


[size=5][b]Source[/b][/size]
Source and earlier versions are on GitHub: [url=https://github.com/KerballOne/ShipbreakerMods]KerballOne/ShipbreakerMods[/url]

